# The tracked SHAPE of the environment. The real .env is untracked and never
# committed — a pre-commit hook refuses any .env* that is not this file.
#
# Every value the application reads must appear here, with a comment saying what
# it is for. A config value that exists only in someone's .env is a value the
# next person's process cannot start without and cannot discover.

# ── Core ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
{{CLI_ENV_PREFIX}}_ENV=development
LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# ── CI semantics ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to 1 by CI and by `{{CLI}} test --ci`. Under it, an env-gate skip becomes a
# test failure: CI guarantees the environment, so a skip means the harness broke.
# {{CI_ENV_VAR}}=1

# ── Scheduled jobs: dead-man switches ───────────────────────────────────
# One push URL per job. A job pings it on success AND on a legitimate decline —
# an executed-and-declined job must stay distinguishable from a dead cron, or
# every correct decline pages somebody and the pages stop being read.
#
# A job with no monitor behind it is a job that can stop running silently, which
# is the failure mode this whole system exists to remove. tests/test_reporting_jobs.py
# fails if a registered job's variable is missing from this file.
HEARTBEAT_REPO_REPORT=

# ── Scheduled jobs: where a finding goes ────────────────────────────────
# Incoming webhook for the channel that receives escalations. Empty disables
# notification without disabling the jobs — the ledger still records everything.
NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_URL=
